# Add project specific R8 rules here.
# AGP will combine all keep rule files in src/main/keepRules to pass to R8
#
# For more details, see
#   https://d.android.com/r/tools/r8/keep-rules

# If your project uses WebView with JS, uncomment the following
# and specify the fully qualified class name to the JavaScript interface
# class:
#-keepclassmembers class fqcn.of.javascript.interface.for.webview {
#   public *;
#}

# --- Project rules (kept deliberately narrow; see docs/architecture.md, "Release build (R8)") ---
#
# Already covered by consumer rules shipped inside the libraries, so NOT repeated here:
#   kotlinx.serialization (Companion/serializer()/$$serializer for @Serializable DTOs), Retrofit 3
#   (service interfaces + suspend/generic signatures), OkHttp, Coil, Hilt, DataStore.

# Navigation 3 restores the back stack by serializing each NavKey polymorphically and re-resolving
# its class by NAME with reflection after process death / rotation. If R8 renames or removes a
# NavKey implementation, the saved name no longer resolves and restoration crashes. Only the few
# route classes are affected; their serializers are retained by the kotlinx.serialization rules.
-keep class * implements androidx.navigation3.runtime.NavKey
